    "slug": "send-full-quality-photos-on-whatsapp",
    "title": "WhatsApp ruins your photos: how to send full-quality photos to clients",
    "seoTitle": "How to send full-quality photos on WhatsApp",
    "description": "Why WhatsApp makes wedding photos look soft, what the HD option really does, how to send originals as documents, and when to use a link instead.",
    "author": "bharat",
    "date": "2026-10-18",
    "category": "delivery",
    "image": "/blog/og/send-full-quality-photos-on-whatsapp.png",
    "html": "<p>Photographers spend hours editing a photo, send it on WhatsApp, and the client sees a soft, blotchy version on their phone. That is not the edit. WhatsApp compresses photos to save data, and most clients never know there is another way.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-short-answer\">The short answer</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For a few photos, send them <strong>as a Document</strong>. WhatsApp sends the original file without compressing it.</li>\n<li>The <strong>HD option</strong> looks sharper than the default but is still compressed.</li>\n<li>For more than a handful of photos, send a <strong>gallery link</strong> instead of the files.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"why-whatsapp-reduces-quality\">Why WhatsApp reduces quality</h2>\n<p>When you send a photo normally, WhatsApp shrinks its resolution and file size so it sends quickly on mobile data. A 20 MB edited file can arrive as a small fraction of that. Fine detail in jewellery, lehenga embroidery and skin tones is the first thing to go.</p>\n<h2 id=\"option-1-the-hd-button\">Option 1: the HD button</h2>\n<p>When you attach a photo, WhatsApp shows an HD option. It sends a larger, sharper version than the default.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Good for:</strong> quick previews where speed matters.</li>\n<li><strong>Limit:</strong> it is still compressed, so it is not the file you edited.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"option-2-send-as-a-document\">Option 2: send as a Document</h2>\n<p>Instead of attaching from the gallery, attach the photo as a Document. WhatsApp then sends the original file unchanged, up to 2 GB per file.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Good for:</strong> a few final photos, such as a favourite portrait the couple wants to print.</li>\n<li><strong>Limits:</strong> the client sees a file icon instead of a preview, it uses more of their data, and sending hundreds of documents is not practical.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"option-3-send-a-link\">Option 3: send a link</h2>\n<p>For a full set, send one link to a gallery or folder. The client views photos at full quality and downloads what they need.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Good for:</strong> previews of a whole function, the complete wedding, or sharing with the family.</li>\n<li><strong>Limit:</strong> a plain folder link is hard to use on a phone with thousands of photos. A gallery made for clients is easier. Compare the options in <a href=\"/blog/how-to-deliver-wedding-photos-to-clients-india\">pen drive, Google Drive or online gallery</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"which-to-use-when\">Which to use when</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Situation</th>\n<th>Best way</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Two or three teaser photos on the wedding night</td>\n<td>HD button</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A few final photos for printing</td>\n<td>Send as Document</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A full function or the whole wedding</td>\n<td>Gallery link</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Every guest wants their own photos</td>\n<td>Face search gallery link</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3 id=\"does-whatsapp-hd-send-original-quality\">Does WhatsApp HD send original quality?</h3>\n<p>No. HD sends a sharper version than the default, but the photo is still compressed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"how-do-i-send-a-photo-on-whatsapp-without-losing-quality\">How do I send a photo on WhatsApp without losing quality?</h3>\n<p>Attach it as a Document instead of as a photo. WhatsApp sends the original file unchanged.</p>\n<h3 id=\"what-is-the-maximum-file-size-for-a-whatsapp-document\">What is the maximum file size for a WhatsApp document?</h3>\n<p>WhatsApp allows documents of up to 2 GB per file.</p>\n<h3 id=\"what-is-the-best-way-to-send-hundreds-of-wedding-photos\">What is the best way to send hundreds of wedding photos?</h3>\n<p>A link to an online gallery. It keeps full quality, works on phones, and avoids hundreds of separate files in a chat.</p>\n",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Does WhatsApp HD send original quality?",
        "a": "No. HD sends a sharper version than the default, but the photo is still compressed."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I send a photo on WhatsApp without losing quality?",
        "a": "Attach it as a Document instead of as a photo. WhatsApp sends the original file unchanged."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the maximum file size for a WhatsApp document?",
        "a": "WhatsApp allows documents of up to 2 GB per file."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the best way to send hundreds of wedding photos?",
        "a": "A link to an online gallery. It keeps full quality, works on phones, and avoids hundreds of separate files in a chat."
      }
    ],
